WEBVTT

00:01.540 --> 00:04.510
In matters relating
to the world of the dead

00:04.610 --> 00:07.970
there is an institution that judges
the sins of the deceased

00:08.230 --> 00:09.770
the Ju-Oh-Cho.

00:10.610 --> 00:12.380
The Summons Section
of the Judgment Bureau

00:12.480 --> 00:16.210
comprises a group supporting
the ministry's operating functions

00:16.320 --> 00:19.150
by guiding the lost souls
that wander the mortal world.

00:19.520 --> 00:21.150
They are also known as...

00:21.390 --> 00:23.830
the Shinigami.

00:24.090 --> 00:30.760
nureta hitomi no oku

00:24.090 --> 00:30.760
Deep behind its wavering stare

00:32.470 --> 00:42.780
aoi tsuki wa shizuka ni koboreochiteyuku

00:32.470 --> 00:42.780
The pale moon quietly descends

00:32.550 --> 00:41.800
Yami no Matsuei

00:49.090 --> 00:54.960
azayaka na sekai wa

00:49.090 --> 00:54.960
The splendid world

00:57.330 --> 01:07.400
oto mo naku shizuka ni yami ni kieteyuku

00:57.330 --> 01:07.400
Disappears into the darkness without a sound

01:07.500 --> 01:15.140
byouyomi no naka kakemeguru yami no naka o

01:07.500 --> 01:15.140
Running about in the dark as time runs out

01:15.240 --> 01:21.770
soshite aratanaru toki o mukae ima

01:15.240 --> 01:21.770
A new era beckons now

01:24.490 --> 01:29.580
kizutsuita kuroi tsubasa

01:24.490 --> 01:29.580
The injured black wings

01:29.760 --> 01:36.130
tsuki no akari ni terasarete

01:29.760 --> 01:36.130
Shine in the moonlight

01:36.730 --> 01:40.930
utsukushiku maiagare

01:36.730 --> 01:40.930
Rising upward in a beautiful dance

01:41.070 --> 01:46.270
shinku no kuchizuke ga ima

01:41.070 --> 01:46.270
The crimson kiss

01:46.380 --> 01:53.210
kokoro no oku ni nagarekomu

01:46.380 --> 01:53.210
Flows deeply into the soul

01:53.380 --> 01:59.180
soshite yume no naka e

01:53.380 --> 01:59.180
Penetrating into one's dreams

02:09.330 --> 02:10.730
Who's that?

02:11.840 --> 02:15.900
Um, Dr. Muraki hasn't come to
see me for my regular check-up.

02:16.010 --> 02:19.570
I went to his cabin, but it was locked.
And there was no answer.

02:19.680 --> 02:20.940
It couldn't be...!

02:35.730 --> 02:36.890
Doctor?

02:52.380 --> 02:53.540
Muraki...

02:54.150 --> 02:57.710
No... this can't be! Doctor!

02:57.880 --> 02:59.750
<i>What on earth is going on?!</i>

02:59.850 --> 03:01.880
<i>How could Muraki have been killed?!</i>

03:01.800 --> 03:06.810
Episode 8: The King of Swords, Part 2

03:15.670 --> 03:18.070
No... Doctor!

03:19.570 --> 03:20.600
Princess Tsubaki!

03:25.510 --> 03:28.040
I can't believe Muraki is dead.

03:31.380 --> 03:34.350
I performed the autopsy.

03:34.450 --> 03:37.980
I'm still only a student, so I might
not be as thorough as Dr. Muraki.

03:38.260 --> 03:40.990
Let's see. The cause of Dr. Muraki's death is

03:41.090 --> 03:43.560
as I thought, poison in the wine he was drinking.

03:43.960 --> 03:48.460
The time of death was between
2 and 3:30 in the morning.

03:48.570 --> 03:52.440
However, two things make this
different from Wakabayashi-san.

03:52.540 --> 03:55.840
The first is that his heart was not removed.

03:55.940 --> 03:57.430
He still had his heart?

03:57.540 --> 03:59.770
Yes. The other difference is that

03:59.880 --> 04:06.340
something in the envelope found
on him was for some reason torn in two.

04:08.490 --> 04:10.720
"To my love, Princess Tsubaki."

04:10.820 --> 04:14.050
"This is a gift from one who truly loves you."

04:14.160 --> 04:17.490
"The two dark gentlemen who lie
in the rose covered casket...

04:17.600 --> 04:19.430
the King of Swords."

04:20.630 --> 04:23.730
The King of Swords ripped in two, huh?

04:24.040 --> 04:26.160
I've had enough!
I can't take this anymore!

04:26.270 --> 04:28.640
Please take the ship back to port, Kakyouin-san.

04:28.740 --> 04:31.770
There have been two murders already!
We have to head back!

04:31.880 --> 04:34.070
I can't do that.

04:34.180 --> 04:36.980
If it became known there
were murders on my ship...

04:38.050 --> 04:41.280
Is making money more important than our lives?!

04:41.390 --> 04:42.720
- Sir!
- What's the matter?

04:42.820 --> 04:44.980
The bridge tells me that

04:45.090 --> 04:47.680
we're not able to make wireless contact.

04:47.790 --> 04:51.820
D-Does that mean we're stranded
in the middle of the ocean?!

04:51.930 --> 04:53.300
Well, uh...

04:53.730 --> 04:54.960
You've got to be kidding!

04:55.170 --> 04:57.100
Just get us back into port immediately!

04:57.200 --> 04:59.300
Th-That's easy to say, but...

04:59.400 --> 05:03.170
it would be more dangerous for
us to take an unplanned course.

05:03.280 --> 05:05.610
Oh, really? All right then.

05:05.710 --> 05:07.300
Listen, Kakyouin-san.

05:07.410 --> 05:09.350
If I were to get killed here

05:09.450 --> 05:12.380
you can be sure I'd haunt you to death!

05:16.120 --> 05:19.110
W-Well, I'll be on my way too.

05:22.790 --> 05:24.160
Oh, right.

05:24.260 --> 05:26.960
There's something I want to ask you, sir.

05:27.070 --> 05:29.800
What is it? Make it quick.

05:29.900 --> 05:32.730
I heard a strange rumor about
a woman called Eileen.

05:32.840 --> 05:34.400
I know nothing of it!

05:34.510 --> 05:39.140
Huh? Well, I heard that
she vanished from this ship.

05:39.880 --> 05:42.470
Rumors are nothing more than rumors.

05:42.580 --> 05:45.020
Tsuzuki-kun...

05:45.780 --> 05:48.780
- Are you done with me?
- Yes.

05:53.360 --> 05:55.790
<i>The owner is hiding something.</i>

05:55.890 --> 05:58.090
<i>The murders and the tarot cards...</i>

05:58.200 --> 06:00.100
<i>the messages to Princess Tsubaki...</i>

06:00.200 --> 06:02.960
<i>and the disappearance of Eileen.</i>

06:03.070 --> 06:06.090
<i>What on earth is happening on this ship?</i>

06:13.280 --> 06:15.300
<i>Muraki is dead.</i>

06:17.450 --> 06:19.850
<i>The man who had killed me--</i>

06:23.620 --> 06:25.350
<i>But who did it?</i>

06:25.460 --> 06:27.580
<i>And for what purpose?</i>

06:28.130 --> 06:31.890
<i>The message left at the murder
was addressed to Princess Tsubaki.</i>

06:32.000 --> 06:35.090
<i>Hisoka, you stay close by Princess Tsubaki.</i>

06:35.200 --> 06:37.760
<i>You protect her from danger.
All right?</i>

06:40.340 --> 06:43.570
No! This can't be! Doctor!

06:43.680 --> 06:45.440
- Princess Tsubaki!
- Doctor!

06:45.540 --> 06:46.940
Oh, no!

06:56.350 --> 06:58.450
<i>This man will be your doctor.</i>

06:58.560 --> 07:00.580
<i>Doctor?</i>

07:00.690 --> 07:02.160
<i>Nice to meet you.</i>

07:02.990 --> 07:04.430
<i>This is for Tsubaki.</i>

07:05.000 --> 07:06.590
<i>- Your heart is...
- No!</i>

07:07.130 --> 07:08.660
<i>All of these memories flooding in!</i>

07:09.070 --> 07:10.900
<i>Are you going to take me to Japan?</i>

07:11.000 --> 07:13.970
<i>Of course!
We're friends after all!</i>

07:15.510 --> 07:17.030
<i>Eileen?</i>

07:18.610 --> 07:22.770
<i>Where are you? Eileen?
Hey, where did you go?</i>

07:22.880 --> 07:25.150
<i>This is beyond my control!</i>

07:29.050 --> 07:32.110
<i>Doctor! Doctor!</i>

07:33.760 --> 07:37.720
<i>No! I'm overloading!</i>

07:46.540 --> 07:48.400
Hey, how's it going?

07:49.340 --> 07:50.310
Hisoka!

07:54.750 --> 07:57.440
So, you heard from Tatsumi?

07:57.550 --> 07:58.680
That's right.

07:58.780 --> 08:02.740
He said there's been a big increase
in missing people in Hong Kong.

08:02.850 --> 08:04.340
Hong Kong?

08:04.460 --> 08:07.760
Does that have anything to do with
the anomalies at the Hall of Candles?

08:07.860 --> 08:09.420
It does.

08:09.730 --> 08:12.700
The times of the incidents
at the Hall of Candles

08:12.800 --> 08:16.200
and of the disappearances
match perfectly. See?

08:19.470 --> 08:22.460
Right? And if you combine that

08:22.570 --> 08:26.140
with the times when the ship was in Hong Kong...

08:27.580 --> 08:30.210
Gushoushin, send this e-mail right away.

08:30.320 --> 08:34.580
See if a girl by the name of Eileen
is on the list of missing persons.

08:34.690 --> 08:36.520
- Right away.
- And also...

08:36.620 --> 08:38.250
If this is the beginning

08:38.360 --> 08:41.220
what is the meaning of the card
that's been ripped in two?

08:41.330 --> 08:44.190
What is the meaning of the King of Swords?

08:45.430 --> 08:49.990
"A counselor" or "a cruel man."
Since it was ripped in two,

08:50.100 --> 08:54.370
I searched based on the proper
sequence as well as the reverse.

08:55.370 --> 08:58.340
Which meaning are we
supposed to take it as?

09:01.410 --> 09:03.710
Are you all right, Hisoka?

09:03.950 --> 09:05.250
Yeah.

09:09.050 --> 09:10.680
Where are you going, Hisoka-san?

09:10.790 --> 09:13.020
I just need to get some air.

09:18.800 --> 09:21.560
<i>The door to Muraki's room is open!</i>

09:24.340 --> 09:25.630
Doctor...

09:26.240 --> 09:27.570
Princess Tsubaki.

09:30.910 --> 09:33.670
What are you doing here anyway?

09:35.210 --> 09:38.770
I just wanted to see the Doctor's face again.

09:39.920 --> 09:43.120
I've had a weak heart
from the time of my birth.

09:43.220 --> 09:45.160
I used to suffer from spasms.

09:45.260 --> 09:49.850
My father was concerned about it,
so he brought Dr. Muraki to see me.

09:51.330 --> 09:56.560
The first time I met the doctor
was when I was around ten.

10:01.670 --> 10:04.870
I felt as though he was some kind of angel.

10:04.980 --> 10:07.310
He always wore white from top to bottom.

10:07.410 --> 10:11.310
An angel with a silvery stare,
piercing like steel.

10:11.420 --> 10:14.180
I soon developed a crush on the doctor

10:14.290 --> 10:17.520
and I did everything the doctor told me to.

10:17.620 --> 10:20.750
I'd even take my bitter medicine
without complaining.

10:21.790 --> 10:24.420
I wanted to get his approval.

10:25.630 --> 10:28.290
And then this had to happen.

10:29.070 --> 10:31.590
Why did the doctor have to die?

10:31.700 --> 10:33.030
It was punishment.

10:34.910 --> 10:39.140
If he was an angel, his name would
have been "an angel of destruction."

10:39.240 --> 10:42.700
You don't know what he was really like.

10:47.520 --> 10:50.890
You're the one who knows
nothing about the doctor, Azumi.

11:16.080 --> 11:17.950
<i>I've had it! Let's go!</i>

11:18.050 --> 11:20.040
<i>Uh, wait. Sir!</i>

11:20.950 --> 11:22.480
<i>Ow.</i>

11:24.790 --> 11:28.950
Hojo-san, I'm pretty sure that ring
belongs to Wakabayashi-san.

11:29.390 --> 11:30.420
That's right.

11:30.530 --> 11:33.900
There's no point in a dead
man having it, so I'm taking it.

11:35.270 --> 11:37.200
But it doesn't even fit you.

11:37.300 --> 11:42.140
Yes. Well, I'm going to have it
adjusted when I get to Hong Kong.

11:42.240 --> 11:43.400
Good-bye.

11:49.250 --> 11:50.840
Hisoka, is something the matter?

11:50.950 --> 11:52.210
I...

11:53.080 --> 11:56.420
ended up hurting Princess Tsubaki.

11:56.520 --> 12:00.650
I mean, she trusted Muraki
from the bottom of her heart.

12:01.830 --> 12:04.420
She must have it tough.

12:04.530 --> 12:06.900
Her trusted doctor died after all.

12:07.000 --> 12:08.520
But we're talking about Muraki!

12:08.630 --> 12:10.570
I know. But you know...

12:10.670 --> 12:13.400
Muraki may have been our enemy

12:13.510 --> 12:15.670
but for her, he's different.

12:15.770 --> 12:20.210
You've got to consider Princess
Tsubaki's feelings right now.

12:21.350 --> 12:22.310
And so...

12:22.410 --> 12:25.210
if you want to make it up
to her, I can help you out.

12:26.990 --> 12:31.450
Yami no Matsuei

12:33.020 --> 12:34.550
I've got to take my medicine.

12:34.660 --> 12:36.990
I promised the doctor after all.

12:49.370 --> 12:51.570
<i>You can invite Princess Tsubaki to dinner.</i>

12:51.680 --> 12:54.010
<i>Leave the reservations up to me.</i>

12:54.480 --> 12:57.510
<i>You just have to put on a tuxedo and pick her up.</i>

12:57.620 --> 13:00.140
<i>Oh. And don't forget to bring her flowers.</i>

13:01.190 --> 13:02.550
Princess Tsubaki?

13:16.970 --> 13:18.940
Th-This is--

13:23.170 --> 13:25.610
Another message for Princess Tsubaki.

13:25.710 --> 13:27.870
Yes. I found it under the door.

13:32.180 --> 13:33.740
What's this?

13:33.850 --> 13:36.950
Uh, yes.
Hojo-sama kept her clothing in that.

13:45.330 --> 13:47.630
"To my love, Princess Tsubaki."

13:47.730 --> 13:50.930
"This is a gift from one who truly loves you."

13:51.040 --> 13:54.940
"A soulless doll packed away into a box."

13:55.040 --> 13:57.170
"Six of Pentacles."

14:01.680 --> 14:04.380
It's the same as the time
with Wakabayashi-san.

14:04.480 --> 14:07.680
She was poisoned first before
her heart was ripped out.

14:07.790 --> 14:10.080
And the card, of course.

14:14.760 --> 14:16.230
Come to think of it...

14:16.490 --> 14:21.090
I overheard the owner and
Hojo-san arguing last night.

14:21.730 --> 14:24.260
Could it be that
the owner did this?!

14:24.370 --> 14:27.570
No. Father wouldn't do such a thing!

14:27.670 --> 14:29.300
But everybody saw, right?

14:29.410 --> 14:33.070
Hojo-san and the owner were arguing all the time.

14:33.180 --> 14:35.980
We can sort this out by just asking him.

14:36.080 --> 14:37.810
Akiyama-san, where's the owner?

14:37.920 --> 14:40.780
Uh, yes.
The owner is in his quarters.

14:40.890 --> 14:43.910
Let's go!
Everything will become clear then.

14:46.190 --> 14:48.950
<i>This is an announcement from the captain:</i>

14:49.060 --> 14:52.430
<i>Our ship is currently passing
through some rough seas.</i>

14:52.830 --> 14:55.630
<i>As the vessel will pitch considerably,
please be careful.</i>

15:02.940 --> 15:05.030
<i>"To my love, Princess Tsubaki."</i>

15:05.140 --> 15:08.510
<i>"This is a gift from one who truly loves you."</i>

15:08.780 --> 15:09.970
Owner!

15:22.960 --> 15:23.950
Princess Tsubaki!

15:27.970 --> 15:30.230
<i>"The dead speak no words."</i>

15:30.330 --> 15:32.230
<i>"Do you understand it yet?"</i>

15:32.340 --> 15:33.800
<i>"Seven of Wands."</i>

15:40.280 --> 15:42.970
I'm going to be the next to get killed.

15:43.080 --> 15:46.050
I just know it!

15:48.350 --> 15:49.880
Owner...

15:56.030 --> 15:57.150
Father...

16:06.300 --> 16:09.000
<i>The first victim was Wakabayashi Shozo.</i>

16:09.110 --> 16:12.340
<i>The meaning of the Ace of Wands is "the beginning."</i>

16:12.440 --> 16:16.140
<i>The serial murders began
just as the card foretold.</i>

16:16.250 --> 16:19.650
<i>The second victim was Muraki Kazutaka.</i>

16:19.950 --> 16:22.440
<i>The King of Swords card was ripped in two.</i>

16:22.550 --> 16:25.780
<i>Its meaning is that of "a counselor" or "a cruel man."</i>

16:26.060 --> 16:28.720
<i>That must be a description of Muraki himself.</i>

16:29.560 --> 16:32.690
<i>The third victim was Hojo Kanako.</i>

16:32.960 --> 16:36.630
<i>The reverse meaning of the
Six of Pentacles is "to pay a bribe."</i>

16:36.970 --> 16:39.460
<i>Either this ring symbolizes a bribe...</i>

16:39.570 --> 16:41.160
<i>or...</i>

16:41.640 --> 16:45.100
<i>The last of the victims is Kakyouin Takeshi.</i>

16:45.210 --> 16:47.970
<i>The Seven of Wands can also be
read through a reverse sequence.</i>

16:48.080 --> 16:51.170
<i>It means that he was blackmailed.
Which means that...</i>

16:51.280 --> 16:54.620
<i>the owner was being
blackmailed by someone.</i>

16:59.160 --> 17:01.520
But by whom?

17:01.990 --> 17:06.330
The criminal?
He was the only one who knew.

17:06.560 --> 17:09.800
The dead speak no words...
Enough with this game!

17:10.100 --> 17:11.070
Damn!

17:13.700 --> 17:15.800
Why is the criminal killing these people?!

17:15.910 --> 17:17.600
What is the criminal's objective?!

17:17.710 --> 17:21.170
Leaving cards like that,
is this supposed to be a game?!

17:21.280 --> 17:22.300
Tsuzuki-san!

17:22.680 --> 17:24.980
I have a response from
the summons department.

17:25.080 --> 17:27.920
It's concerning that girl Eileen.

17:28.720 --> 17:31.850
How are you feeling, Princess Tsubaki?

17:31.960 --> 17:34.050
I can't say I feel too good.

17:34.660 --> 17:37.960
I'm really sorry about your father.

17:38.060 --> 17:41.620
Please don't remind me again.

17:42.300 --> 17:47.030
There was definitely an Eileen
in the missing persons list.

17:47.140 --> 17:49.040
- Is she dead or alive?
- It's unknown.

17:49.140 --> 17:53.770
She's on the register,
but her soul hasn't returned.

17:53.880 --> 17:56.850
It seems that's the case
with everyone on the list.

17:56.950 --> 18:00.610
In other words, we don't
know if she's dead or alive.

18:00.820 --> 18:03.150
Huh?
Where did you get that ring?

18:03.250 --> 18:04.220
Oh.

18:04.320 --> 18:07.380
I thought maybe I'd return
it to its rightful owner.

18:14.700 --> 18:17.100
Wh-What did you do that for?!

18:17.200 --> 18:20.170
I was only holding it gently.

18:21.210 --> 18:22.700
What is this?

18:23.310 --> 18:25.470
It's a microchip.

18:28.510 --> 18:30.240
What terrible weather.

18:30.350 --> 18:32.750
I'm sorry about before, Princess Tsubaki.

18:33.650 --> 18:36.950
I didn't even consider your feelings

18:37.050 --> 18:39.110
and I said something that hurt you.

18:39.320 --> 18:40.810
Don't worry about it.

18:41.190 --> 18:42.350
But...

18:42.660 --> 18:43.990
tell me, Azumi...

18:44.100 --> 18:47.500
what happened between the two of you?

18:49.830 --> 18:51.320
You should have seen

18:51.440 --> 18:53.730
the look in your eyes as
you stared at the doctor.

18:53.840 --> 18:55.930
It was as cold as ice.

18:56.040 --> 18:57.800
You knew each other, right?

18:57.910 --> 18:59.930
Then why?

19:00.240 --> 19:02.770
- I'm not Hibiki Azumi.
- What?

19:03.210 --> 19:05.010
I'm not even human.

19:05.280 --> 19:07.220
I was killed by Muraki.

19:07.320 --> 19:09.840
I am one who no longer lives in this world.

19:11.220 --> 19:13.620
You're not human?

19:18.260 --> 19:21.320
He came after me after
I witnessed one of his murders

19:21.430 --> 19:23.160
and he put a spell on me.

19:23.970 --> 19:27.060
He took my memory away from me then

19:27.170 --> 19:30.200
and tormented me for three years...

19:31.480 --> 19:33.030
only to kill me in the end.

19:45.790 --> 19:47.880
I am a Shinigami.

19:47.990 --> 19:51.260
I am a Shinigami who wanted
revenge against Muraki.

19:52.260 --> 19:55.600
I don't believe that.

19:58.000 --> 20:01.490
If you doubt me, I'll prove it to you.

20:02.640 --> 20:04.300
What are you going to do?!

20:05.280 --> 20:06.640
Don't!

20:30.970 --> 20:33.730
In order to solve a particular case,

20:33.840 --> 20:37.710
I used Azumi's name to get onto this ship.

20:37.840 --> 20:41.240
I pretended to be a regular human being

20:41.350 --> 20:43.910
and spied on all of you.

20:44.120 --> 20:45.080
I'm sorry.

20:45.550 --> 20:49.010
I'm sorry for lying to you
for all this time. I'm sorry.

20:49.120 --> 20:50.090
Azumi...

20:56.690 --> 21:01.760
How could you hate someone
so much even in death?

21:02.300 --> 21:05.030
To suffer the burden of that hatred

21:05.140 --> 21:10.010
only means that you're not
able to free yourself from him.

21:10.570 --> 21:12.440
Just like me.

21:13.110 --> 21:14.540
Princess Tsubaki...

21:39.460 --> 21:42.460
Next Episode

21:41.910 --> 21:43.810
The first break in solving this case

21:43.910 --> 21:46.000
seems to be drifting away with the tide.

21:46.110 --> 21:49.050
I still can't believe that
Muraki could've died.

21:49.150 --> 21:50.880
The Kings of Swords.

21:50.980 --> 21:53.420
As the tarot cards tell their story

21:53.520 --> 21:56.150
a white angel descends upon this world.

21:57.290 --> 22:00.380
Could it have been you?!

22:00.310 --> 22:09.410
Episode 9     The King of Swords, Part 3

22:00.490 --> 22:05.020
Next time on Yami no Matsuei: The King of Swords, Part 3

22:05.730 --> 22:08.250
Those who live in the darkness wander aimlessly.

22:17.740 --> 22:21.100
arumikan no marui en o mashikaku ni orinagara

22:17.740 --> 22:21.100
As I square the round edges on the drink

22:21.210 --> 22:24.140
kimi o matsu machikado sa

22:21.210 --> 22:24.140
I wait for you on the street corner

22:24.240 --> 22:27.730
nakami no ekitai wa mou nurukute nomenai kedo

22:24.240 --> 22:27.730
The liquid inside is warm and I can't drink it anymore

22:27.850 --> 22:30.440
shikatanaku motsu ore sa

22:27.850 --> 22:30.440
But what can I do but hold onto to it?

22:30.550 --> 22:37.780
yami no naka de ore o utsusu
garasu keesu ni kazarareta

22:30.550 --> 22:37.780
In the glass case reflecting me in the darkness

22:37.890 --> 22:44.520
ningyou ga sakki kara kowai
kao de ore o miteru

22:37.890 --> 22:44.520
There is a doll that has been scowling at me

22:57.980 --> 23:04.400
ore no fuku kuchibue wa wari
to akarui uta de

22:57.980 --> 23:04.400
The tune I whistle is a bright and cheerful one

23:04.920 --> 23:10.850
zensekai no hitotachi ni
sasagerareta noizu

23:04.920 --> 23:10.850
A little noise dedicated to the people of the world

23:11.620 --> 23:17.960
dare hitori shiru hazu
no nai kono merodi ga

23:11.620 --> 23:17.960
No one could possibly recognize the melody

23:18.710 --> 23:24.110
omae ni wa kikoeru ka? Sayonara da
Love me

23:18.710 --> 23:24.110
But do you hear it?
Good-bye, Love me
